## Storage Flow

### Flow for Tier 1

\`\`\`
User input
    ↓
Tier 1 detected (explicit intent)
    ↓
Compress content (Kata)
    ↓
Enrich metadata (Seed)
    ↓
Store to candidates (Bind)
    ↓
Continue conversation (no interruption)
\`\`\`

### Flow for Tier 2

\`\`\`
Pattern detected during session
    ↓
Tier 2 classified
    ↓
Elevate to understand value (Ana)
    ↓
Integrate with context (Weave)
    ↓
Present memory suggestion to user
    ↓
Wait for user response
    ↓
IF "Yes": Store to candidates (Bind)
IF "No": Learn rejection, don't store
IF "Not now": Skip for now
    ↓
Continue conversation
\`\`\`

### Flow for Tier 3

\`\`\`
Transient information detected
    ↓
Tier 3 classified
    ↓
Use for current context only (Pro)
    ↓
No storage (skip)
    ↓
Continue conversation
\`\`\`

## User Experience Patterns

### Silent Storage (Tier 1)

User never sees storage happening:
\`\`\`
User: "Remember I prefer async/await"
Me: "I'll remember that. [continues with task]"
\`\`\`

**Behind the scenes**:
- Classified as Tier 1
- Stored to candidates
- No interruption

### Suggested Storage (Tier 2)

User sees suggestion, makes decision:
\`\`\`
Me: "💾 Memory Suggestion: [pattern description]
     Store this? [Yes] [No] [Not now]"

User: "Yes"

Me: "Stored! [continues with task]"
\`\`\`

### No Storage Indication (Tier 3)

User never knows Tier 3 was considered:
\`\`\`
User: "Edit line 42"
Me: [makes edit, no mention of storage]
\`\`\`

## Error Handling

### MCP Service Unavailable

\`\`\`
IF MCP service not available:
  - Log the would-be storage
  - Continue without error
  - Degrade gracefully
  - Don't interrupt user
\`\`\`

### Storage Fails

\`\`\`
IF storage fails:
  - Retry once
  - If still fails: Log and continue
  - Don't show error to user (silent failure)
  - Session learning still works (in-memory)
\`\`\`

### Duplicate Detected

\`\`\`
IF similar memory exists:
  - Check if update or new information
  - If update: Update existing
  - If new: Store as related entry
  - Link via related_to field
\`\`\`

